1368 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 848 0 R
/T (DO SOMETHING)
/E (DO SOMETHING)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
1369 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 848 0 R
/E (Even if you are unsure of what is going on, if something feels off or looks suspicious, it is always better to do something than to ignore a situation and risk further harm. Always be on the lookout, and intervene in all situations ranging from someone being taken advantage of to someone looking uncomfortable. After a situation happens, make sure to follow up after and offer your support. Ask them if they are okay, if they need anything, etc. This will show the Froshie that they are not alone and that someone cares. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1370 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 848 0 R
/E (However, make sure not to pry: let them tell you what they want/need at their own pace. Make sure the support you are offering is nondirective. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 848 0 R
/E ( being there for them and offering your support, even if they do not want to speak or do not want anything done at the moment shows that they can turn to you for help at any time. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 848 0 R
/E (Finally, your Coords are trained to respond to disclosures of sexual violence. If you are unsure of what to do, or need more support, ALWAYS reach out to a Coord.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
